<title>BELGIUM: SOLVAY OPENS U.S. AUTO-PARTS PLANT.</title>
<headline>SOLVAY OPENS U.S. AUTO-PARTS PLANT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Solvay Automotive Inc., a unit of Belgian chemical group Solvay SA, inaugurated on Thursday a new $80 million (2.4 billion Belgian franc) production facility in Adrian, Michigan, Solvay said in a statement.</p>
<p>The unit will make plastic fuel tanks and composite intake manifolds for customers Chrysler and General Motors.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
